<title>AUSTRIA: Creditanstalt details 1996 results.</title>
<headline>Creditanstalt details 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31.</p>
<p>(Figures in billions of schillings unless stated)</p>
<p>						    1996     1995</p>
<p> Net interest income			  19.331   17.342</p>
<p> Income from securities and investments  2.468    2.230</p>
<p> Net fee and commission income	     3.894    3.553</p>
<p> Net profit on trading activities	  1.679    1.657</p>
<p> Group operating income		     19.331   17.342</p>
<p> Staff expenses				  6.938    6.151</p>
<p> Other administrative expenses	     4.682    4.088</p>
<p> Group operating costs			12.863   11.203</p>
<p> Group operating profit			6.468    6.138</p>
<p> Group pretax profit			   3.399    2.586</p>
<p> Group net profit				2.930    2.166</p>
<p> Total assets				  687.6    645.0</p>
<p> EPS (schillings)			     70.3     51.7</p>
<p> Dividend per share (schillings)	   12	10</p>
<p> Dividend payout ratio (percent)	   17.1    19.3</p>
<p> Return on equity (percent)		  10.8     8.6</p>
<p> Return on assets				 0.44    0.34</p>
<p> Total workforce			    9,845    9,661</p>
<p>NOTES - Full company name is Creditanstalt-Bankverein AG.</p>
<p>According to Austrian accounting standards, operating profit is calculated before risk provisions, which fell to 3.1 billion schillings in 1996 from 3.4 billion a year earlier. Creditanstalt is majority controlled by Bank Austria, which in January acquired two-thirds of the bank's voting shares from the Republic of Austria for 17.2 billion schillings.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +431 53112 274</p>
</text>
